  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 1.2. Increased institutional capacity of workers&#x2019; organizations</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">The National Trade Union Congress of Belize (NTUCB) adopted a Strategic Plan 2023-2028 in June 2023. The plan includes a set of policy decisions and priorities aimed at addressing the crisis brought about by the COVID-19 pandemic, through increased influence of NTUCB in revision of labour legislation. The trade union strategy is to advocate, negotiate and agitate for the enactment and amendment of relevant labour legislation as well as the ratification of ILO Conventions to achieve the complete reform of the legislative framework related to labour. Priority will be given to the OSH legislation, the social security legislation and legislation related to the termination of employment. The ILO provided technical support to NTUCB to evaluate the previous strategic plan, to establish a Trade Union Organizational Capacity (TUOC) framework in order to 
learn about the capacity of the Union in three main areas (internal organizational capacity, capacities to relate and capacities to influence and deliver), looking both at internal and external factors that affect the functioning of the union and to develop a new one, including through consultations with affiliates. The consultations took place virtually in November 2022 and in person in June 2023. The ILO did also provide NTUCB with monitoring and evaluation tools as well as training on development of annual implementation plans.</narrative>
   </description>
